      ["Choose the grammatically correct sentence:", ["She cans dance.", "She can dances.", "She can dance.", "She can to dance."], 2, "After 'can', the main verb stays in its base form: 'dance'."],
      ["What does 'can't' mean?", ["Cannot", "Could", "Maybe", "Must"], 0, "'Can't' is the contraction of 'cannot' and expresses inability or prohibition."],
      ["Complete: 'When I was younger, I ___ run very fast.'", ["May", "Could", "Might", "Must"], 1, "'Could' can express an ability someone had in the past."],
      ["Which modal is commonly used to make a polite request?", ["Must", "Can't", "Could", "Shouldn't"], 2, "'Could' is commonly used to make polite requests."]
